## Phase 2: Resident Data Model
- [ ] Collect fortress residents with `dfhack.units.getCitizens(false, true)`.
- [ ] Reject non-fortress or unloaded-map contexts with a clear message.
- [ ] Build resident rows with unit pointer, readable name, profession, position, traits, and mental attributes.
- [ ] Use DFHack readable-name helpers for display.
- [ ] Use `dfhack.units.getMentalAttrValue()` for effective mental/soul attribute values.

## Phase 3: Search and Filter Engine
- [ ] Implement text search over resident names.
- [ ] Define data-driven filter descriptors for personality traits.
- [ ] Define data-driven filter descriptors for mental/soul attributes.
- [ ] Support `>=`, `<=`, and `between` comparisons.
- [ ] Combine multiple active filters with `AND`.
- [ ] Add default thresholds: high is `>= 75`, low is `<= 25`.

## Phase 4: In-Game Panel UI
- [ ] Create a `gui.ZScreen` opened by the `dwarfsearch` command.
- [ ] Add a search field for resident name filtering.
- [ ] Add controls for selecting trait and mental attribute filters.
- [ ] Add a result list using DFHack GUI widgets.
- [ ] Add a selected-resident details area.
- [ ] Add refresh and close actions.
